    "result_text": "The sheet's due-total and overdue-total now leave out the single highest and single lowest person's figure when three or more people have one. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 acceptance tests.\n\nThe totals are worked out in two places, and I changed both the same way:\n\n- **Server** (`RollupService.java`): the totals written to the `TOTALS` audit line are now trimmed. Since a `TOTALS` line is only written when the totals move, a change can now leave them the same and write no `TOTALS` line. That happens in the test after the cap is set.\n- **Front end**: a new `trimmedSum` helper in `rates.ts` drives the totals row and the header in `people.ts`. A due-total of n/a doesn't count as a figure. For the overdue-total, every person now counts, at 0.00 if nothing of theirs is overdue. Before, only people with an overdue claim were added up, which would have trimmed the wrong figures.\n\nPer-person figures, per-grade and per-period totals, backing and the claimed total are not trimmed. No stored data or schema changes were needed.",
